Helios DXVK fork: flush-gate points that shared allocations publish

Conduit guest/windows/docs/shared-surfaces.md section 4 and
docs/flush-gate.md section 9. Applied after 0005 by
ci/windows/Build-Driver.ps1.

The HEFL flush gate withholds the releaser's WDDM fence, but nothing orders
the acquirer behind it: dxgkrnl's keyed mutex holds only the acquirer's DMA
buffers, and a D3D11 device on Venus reads through the Venus ring. The
existing consumer wait does order it (an imported image's read waits for its
allocation producer's announced epoch, heliosPresentWaitBeforeRefresh), as
long as the releaser publishes an epoch at the hand-off.

- D3D11ImmediateContext::HeliosSignalFlushPointTracked: the flush point's
  signal, with one HeliosProducerOperation retained per allocation the UMD
  then publishes the point on, so a waiter is failed rather than hung if the
  signal is never submitted.

diff --git a/src/d3d11/d3d11_context_imm.cpp b/src/d3d11/d3d11_context_imm.cpp
index 26744591..22556a5c 100644
--- a/src/d3d11/d3d11_context_imm.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d11/d3d11_context_imm.cpp
@@ -1243,6 +1243,26 @@ namespace dxvk {
   }
 
 
+  uint64_t D3D11ImmediateContext::HeliosSignalFlushPointTracked(
+    const Rc<DxvkFence>&        Fence,
+          uint64_t              Value,
+          std::vector<Rc<HeliosProducerOperation>> Operations) {
+    D3D10DeviceLock lock = LockContext();
+
+    EmitCs([
+      cFence = Fence,
+      cValue = Value,
+      cOperations = std::move(Operations)
+    ] (DxvkContext* ctx) {
+      for (const auto& operation : cOperations)
+        ctx->trackProducer(operation);
+      ctx->signalFence(cFence, cValue);
+    });
+    ExecuteFlush(GpuFlushType::ExplicitFlush, nullptr, false);
+    return GetCurrentSequenceNumber();
+  }
+
+
   void D3D11ImmediateContext::HeliosSignalPresentFence(
     const Rc<DxvkFence>&        Fence,
           uint64_t              Value,
